-- title:
--   Injectivity of Vélu's abscissa map on ψ₂²-roots
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field in which $2 \neq 0$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $L$ that is elliptic. Let $n$ be a natural number and let $Q$ be a point of the associated affine curve $W$ whose additive order is exactly $2n+1$. Put $S = \{\,(k \bullet Q).\text{coordsOrZero} : 1 \le k \le n\,\}$, the image in $L \times L$ of the interval $[1,n]$ under the map sending $k$ to the affine coordinates of $k \bullet Q$ (the point at infinity being sent to $(0,0)$), and let $X_S(x) = x + \sum_{P \in S} \bigl( t_P/(x - P_1) + u_P/(x - P_1)^2 \bigr)$ be Vélu's abscissa function `veluX`, where $t_P = 2 G_x(P) - a_1 G_y(P)$ and $u_P = G_y(P)^2$ in the notation of the project's Vélu data. Assume $r, r' \in L$ are both roots of the polynomial $\Psi_2^2$ of $W$ (the square of the second division polynomial, $4x^3 + b_2 x^2 + 2b_4 x + b_6$), and that $X_S(r) = X_S(r')$. The conclusion is $r = r'$.
--
--   This is the injectivity of Vélu's $x$-coordinate map, restricted to the abscissae of the $2$-torsion of $W$, for the Vélu summing set of a cyclic subgroup of odd order $2n+1$ generated by $Q$. It is used to show that the Vélu quotient of $W$ by such a subgroup has non-vanishing discriminant, i.e. that the quotient Weierstrass equation again defines an elliptic curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_veluX_oddOrderSummingSet_injOn_psi2Sq_roots.lean

